# Browser
# What a player sees of a creature blocking more than one attacker (CR 509.1g, 510.1d): Bot2's Ulvenwald Oddity blocks
# Benalish Hero, banded with Guerrilla Gorilla, and so blocks both (CR 702.22h) - the one way a printed card in the engine
# blocks two attackers until a card that "can block any number of creatures" is added. Bot1's page draws the Oddity once,
# across from both attackers standing side by side, and writes over its art which it blocks. In the damage step the Oddity's
# 4 is divided among the attackers it blocks (by Bot1, through banding, CR 702.22k), each attacker wearing its share: all 4
# on the Hero, which dies, and the Gorilla lives.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Benalish Hero
Guerrilla Gorilla
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Ulvenwald Oddity
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Benalish Hero.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Guerrilla Gorilla.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ulvenwald Oddity.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Benalish Hero > Bot2; Guerrilla Gorilla > Bot2)
Bot1.Choose(Guerrilla Gorilla)
Bot2.Block(Ulvenwald Oddity > Benalish Hero)
[T3 Bot1.Blockers]
? Client.Bot1.OpponentBattlefield.Ulvenwald Oddity.Annotation = Blocking Benalish Hero and Guerrilla Gorilla
? Client.Bot1.Combat = Attacking Bot2: Benalish Hero, Guerrilla Gorilla
Bot1.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Banding: divide their creature's combat damage
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Benalish Hero.Share = 4 damage
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Guerrilla Gorilla.Share = 0 damage
Bot1.AssignDamage(Ulvenwald Oddity > Benalish Hero: 4)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Benalish Hero
Bot1.Battlefield.Guerrilla Gorilla.Damage = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Ulvenwald Oddity.Damage = 3
